  "description": "The meme implicitly references the stereotype that certain groups (in this case, white people) are systematically excluded from spaces, conversations, or perspectives that are deemed important or 'prospective' (forward-looking, future-oriented). This stereotype is rooted in real-world racial dynamics and can be interpreted as a form of exclusionary rhetoric, often used to justify or normalize the absence of white voices in certain contexts.",
